{"title":"Career Roadmap · Assistive Device Consultant","role":"Assistive Device Consultant","summary":"An Assistive Device Consultant helps people identify and use appropriate technologies and devices that improve mobility, independence, communication, positioning, daily living and participation.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Prosthetics & Orthotics"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Assistive Device Consultant is a broad role covering assessment, recommendation, fitting coordination, training and follow-up for assistive products. For regulated prosthetic/orthotic assessment and fabrication responsibilities, the appropriate recognized qualification, registration and scope of practice should be verified under the applicable professional framework."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Assistive Device Consultant helps people identify and use appropriate technologies and devices that improve mobility, independence, communication, positioning, daily living and participation."},{"type":"p","text":"In a Prosthetics & Orthotics pathway, the professional may work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prostheses"},{"text":"Orthoses"},{"text":"Wheelchairs"},{"text":"Walking aids"},{"text":"Mobility devices"},{"text":"Seating systems"},{"text":"Positioning devices"},{"text":"Pressure-relief systems"},{"text":"Adaptive equipment"},{"text":"Rehabilitation technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines clinical assessment, biomechanics, rehabilitation, product knowledge, patient education and device follow-up."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"h","text":"Prosthetics & Orthotics Education"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical + Rehabilitation Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive Technology Exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital / Rehabilitation Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive Device Consultant / Trainee"